DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The functions here are used  within  the  RPC’s  secure  authentication
       mechanism (AUTH_DES).  There should be no need for user programs to use
       this functions.

       The  function kkeeyy__ddeeccrryyppttsseessssiioonn() uses the (remote) server netname and
       takes the DES key for decrypting.  It uses the public key of the server
       and the secret key associated with the effective  UID  of  the  calling
       process.

       The  function  kkeeyy__eennccrryyppttsseessssiioonn()  is  the inverse of kkeeyy__ddeeccrryyppttsseess‐‐
       ssiioonn().  It encrypts the DES keys with the public key of the server and
       the secret key  associated  with  the  effective  UID  of  the  calling
       process.

       The  function  kkeeyy__ggeennddeess()  is  used to ask the keyserver for a secure
       conversation key.

       The function kkeeyy__sseettsseeccrreett() is used to set the key for  the  effective
       UID of the calling process.

       The  function kkeeyy__sseeccrreettkkeeyy__iiss__sseett() can be used to determine whether a
       key has been set for the effective UID of the calling process.

